  "id": "COMPOUND:29936 - PROTEIN:4914",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound (2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-4,5-dihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)-2-[[10-(hydroxymethyl)-4,4,8,14-tetramethyl-17-[5-methyl-1-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2R,3R,4S,5R)-3,4,5-trihydroxyoxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxyhex-4-enyl]-2,3,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]oxy]oxan-3-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol interacts with Replicase polyprotein 1a. This compound is identified as a target of multiple pathways, including Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 1A2 and Cyanovirin-N, which are known to interact with replicase proteins. The evidence suggests that the compound may inhibit the function of Replicase polyprotein 1a through a mechanism involving the transport of anionic molecules, possibly by binding to and disrupting the activity of the transporter. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of transporters suggest a potential role in modulating the activity of replicase proteins, which are critical for viral replication. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that the compound may act as a modulator of replicase activity, potentially offering therapeutic potential in viral infections.",
